-- title:
--   Branch place at a supersingular point of the H₁ chart
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Fixed are a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   **Valuation ring over $q$ and constant reduction.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$ (this is `LiesOverPrime`), and $\kappa_A$ denotes its residue field. $W$ is a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A, M')$ — the subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\kappa_A)$ generated over $\kappa_A$ by the two series `jqModC` and `jqNModC _ M'` — over $\kappa_A$, where a place is a valuation subring containing the image of $\kappa_A$, not equal to the whole field, and a principal ideal ring; the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the places in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,\kappa_A$, i.e. those satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace`. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of intermediate fields of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, that is, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ is contained in $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldBar}(q^2M', \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M')$. $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A, M')$: a valuation subring `integers` of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal of `integers`, the condition that $\mathrm{algebraMap}(x)$ lies in `integers` precisely when $x \in A$, compatibility of the residue with $A \to \kappa_A$, existence for every nonzero $f$ of a scalar $c$ with $c\cdot f$ in `integers` of nonzero residue, together with a map on places preserving degrees and compatible with push-forward of divisors of functions of nonzero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, this image lies in $R_0$.integers and its residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a distinguished element of $W$.
--
--   **The small field of constants.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$; write $A_0 = A \cap k_0$ (formally, the pullback of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$). The hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` state that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that it is a henselian local ring, and that its residue field $\kappa_0$ is algebraically closed; `hκ` states that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Roots of unity and level.** $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity, and `hιξ` provides a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. $H_1$ is the subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ equal to the intersection of $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ (the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$) with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. $K$ is the intermediate field $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0\,(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}(q^2M', H_1))$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$ over $k_0$, i.e. the field generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$; $K$ carries an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $A_0 \to k_0 \to K$. The element $j \in K$ has Laurent series $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\,k_0\,\mathrm{jq}$, the $q$-expansion of the modular $j$-invariant, and is assumed nonzero.
--
--   **Functoriality hypotheses for the rigid $H_1$ datum.** For all $A_0$-algebras $T$: `hℓ` says variable changes carry $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-points to $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-points, where `IsGamma1Point W ℓg D` asserts that $(D.xP, D.yP)$ satisfies the affine equation of $W$, that $\mathrm{preΨ}\,\ell_g$ vanishes at $D.xP$, and that $D.xQ = D.xP$, $D.yQ = D.yP$; `hM` says variable changes carry $\mathrm{IsGamma0PowAt}\,W\,p\,k\,h$ (the two-kernel condition if $p^k = 2$, otherwise the cyclic-generator-kernel condition) to the same condition for $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}$ of $h$ in degree $\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k$; `hL` says divisors of $\mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\,W\,\ell_g\,n\,x$ transform, under $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}$, into divisors of $\mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\,(C\bullet W)\,\ell_g\,n\,(u^{-2}(x - C.r))$.
--
--   **Drinfeld level data.** $\mathcal G$ is a family of relative group laws on the projective models of Weierstrass curves over $A_0$-algebras with unit discriminant, assumed chord–tangent (each group law admits a points evaluation) and origin-normalised (the identity section is cut out on the origin chart by a homomorphism killing $\mathrm{xOverY}$ and $\mathrm{zOverY}$); $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport` for $\mathcal G$ and $q$ — a functorial transport of raw Drinfeld pairs along $A_0$-algebra maps and variable changes, preserving the level condition — assumed to be a section transport, i.e. compatible with the graded homomorphisms implementing variable changes and coefficient maps. The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every projective Weierstrass curve over an $A_0$-algebra, graded ring homomorphisms realising a given variable change (`IsVariableChangeHom`) and a given coefficient map (`IsCoefficientHom`), in each case with the irrelevant ideal of the target contained in the image of the irrelevant ideal of the source.
--
--   **Moduli package and the pinned Tate point.** $P_0$ is an absolute fine moduli package for the level moduli datum attached to $\mathcal R = \mathrm{rigidDataH1Pow}\,A_0\,\ell_g\,M'\,q\,h\ell\,hM\,hL\,\mathcal G\,\mathcal T$ (the rigidification of the product of the $\Gamma_0(M')$-power component, the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-component and the Drinfeld level component, restricted to the locus where `IsGamma1Link` holds): a ring $B_0$ with an $A_0$-algebra structure, a universal point `univ`, and the property that every point over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of `univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $B_0 \to T$. $x_0$ is a point of this datum over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent series $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$. $\mathrm{clC}$ is an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism from $B_0$ to the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j = \mathrm{chartAlg}\,A_0\,K\,\{j\}$, and `hclC` says that composing it with the inclusion into $K$ gives the classifying map of $x_0$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hμ` pins $x_0$ at the Tate curve: there exist a variable change $C$ over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$ and a raw datum $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ such that (i) the class of $r$ is $x_0$; (ii) writing $(x_\ell, y_\ell) = \mathrm{tateToricPoint}\,k_0\,q\,(\xi^q)$ for the unit $\xi^q$ of order $\ell_g$, one has $C.u\,(2x_\ell + 1/6) = 2y_\ell + x_\ell$, $C.r = -1/12$, $C.s = -1/2$, $C.t = 1/24$ (the scalars taken as constant Laurent series); (iii) the base change of $r$'s curve to $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$ is $C \bullet \mathrm{tateBase}\,k_0\,q$; (iv) for every prime $p \mid M'$, every field $F'$, every ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and every primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta \in F'$, the image of the $p$-component $r.\mathrm{level}.1(p)$ under base change to $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}(k_0)$ followed by coefficientwise $f$ equals $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}$ of $C$ (coefficientwise transported by $f$) in degree $\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,v_p(M')$ applied to $\prod_{1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2,\ p \nmid a} (X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\,F'\,q\,\zeta^a)_1)$; (v) the image of the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-slot $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$ is the variable change by $C$ of the level datum $(x_\ell, y_\ell, x_\ell, y_\ell)$; (vi) there exist $P_x, P_y, Q_x, Q_y \in K$ whose Laurent series are the four coordinates of the variable change by $C$ of $\mathrm{cuspData}\,k_0\,q\,(\xi^{\ell_g})\,(1,0)\,(0,-1)$, and the two Drinfeld sections $P$, $Q$ of $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2$ pass through $(P_x, P_y)$ and $(Q_x, Q_y)$ in the sense of `IsSectionThrough`.
--
--   Finally $\theta : \kappa_0 \to \kappa_A$ is a ring homomorphism with $\theta(\mathrm{residue}\,a) = \mathrm{residue}$ of the image of $a$ in $A$, for every $a \in A_0$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every maximal ideal $y$ of the chart algebra $\mathcal C := \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$, every $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $\psi : \mathcal C \to \kappa_0$ whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$ (i.e. $\psi(c) = 0 \iff c \in y$), and every raw datum $x$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\kappa_0$ whose class equals the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\psi \circ \mathrm{clC}$, such that the affine curve of $x$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point over $\kappa_0$ (every $P$ with $q \cdot P = 0$ is $0$), there exist a field $\Omega$ with a $\kappa_A$-algebra structure, a place $V$ of $\Omega$ over $\kappa_A$, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}$ from the residue field of the valuation ring of $V$ to $\kappa_A$, and a ring homomorphism $\rho : \mathcal C \to \mathcal O_V$ such that:
--
--   1. $\mathrm{res}$ is a retraction of the structure map: $\mathrm{res}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,\kappa_A\,\kappa(V)\,c) = c$ for all $c \in \kappa_A$;
--
--   2. for every $a \in A_0$, the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,A_0\,\mathcal C\,a)$ is the image of $\theta(\mathrm{residue}\,a)$ under $\kappa_A \to \Omega$;
--
--   3. for every $c \in \mathcal C$, $\mathrm{res}(\mathrm{residue}(\rho\,c)) = \theta(\psi\,c)$;
--
--   4. the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho(\mathrm{jChartFin}\,A_0\,K\,j)$, that is of $j$, is transcendental over $\kappa_A$;
--
--   5. $\Omega$ is finite-dimensional over the subfield of $\Omega$ generated over $\kappa_A$ by that image of $j$;
--
--   6. there are an $A_0$-algebra structure on $\mathcal O_V$ and an $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $\rho_A : B_0 \to \mathcal O_V$ with $\rho_A(b) = \rho(\mathrm{clC}\,b)$ for all $b \in B_0$, together with a raw datum $x_V$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\mathcal O_V$ whose class is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\rho_A$, and a ring homomorphism $\chi_Q$ from the origin chart ring of the curve of $x_V.\mathrm{level}.2.2$ to $\Omega$ such that the base change of the second Drinfeld section $Q$ along $\mathcal O_V \to \Omega$ — that is, $\mathrm{Spec}$ of $\mathcal O_V \to \Omega$ followed by $Q$ — equals $\mathrm{Spec}\,\chi_Q$ followed by the origin chart inclusion, and $\chi_Q(\mathrm{xOverY}) = 0$, $\chi_Q(\mathrm{zOverY}) = 0$ (so $Q$ becomes the origin over $\Omega$);
--
--   7. and, in addition, there exist $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_1(\ell_g)$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and both diagonal entries $\gamma_{00}$, $\gamma_{11}$ reducing to $0$ in $\mathbb Z/q$, and a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,q\,(\xi^{\ell_g})\,q\,(q^2M')\,H_1\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$ — i.e. for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f, g$ for $\Gamma_{H_1}(q^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$, $p_g$ having nonzero associated series, all $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $p_f/p_g$, and all embeddings $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi^{\ell_g}$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$, the $\iota$-image of $\tau(x)$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}\,q\,\gamma^{-1}$ — such that $\tau$ maps $\mathcal C$ into itself, and for every $h \in \mathcal C$: if for every integer $n$ the $n$-th Laurent coefficient of $\tau(h)$ is the image of an element of the maximal ideal of $A_0$, then the image of $\rho(h)$ in $\Omega$ is $0$.
--
--   This is the construction, in the full-level $H_1$ setting, of a connected branch through a supersingular point of the integral two-chart model of $X_{H_1}(q^2M')$: at a maximal ideal of the chart algebra whose associated curve has no $q$-torsion, it produces a place of a transcendence-degree-one extension of $\kappa_A$ along which the chart reduces compatibly with $\theta$ and $\psi$, on which the second Drinfeld section specialises to the origin, and it exports the level automorphism $\tau$ attached to a matrix $\gamma \in \Gamma_1(\ell_g) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ with diagonal entries divisible by $q$ that cuts out this branch. It feeds the subsequent identification of the branch as a Frobenius moduli place, [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_isModuliPlaceOf_map_frobenius_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_isModuliPlaceOf_map_frobenius_of_forall_evalAt_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1).
